Hi group,

I'm running a comparison of the output metrics from GGIR 1.9.1 to GGIR 1.10 and I'm noticing that some of the calculations differ. I'm using the same input data and GGIR arguments for the two versions.

Below is a summary of differences. My test compares each output CSV and, if any line is not equal between the versions, it fails on that file. Therefore some files fail on the header and some on the first data row.

https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1rRb6kmd0YUFtWetGDF98Lruf5AeEqXDlg-VnXTCAWcU/edit?usp=sharing

Dataset and results:
https://drive.google.com/open?id=1SYQxZPjbViVs7RbnD57ZSX8pzeue0V_q

Does anyone know what I might be doing wrong?

Regards,
Mark

