Hi Mark,

Part 2:
When argument winhr =c(5,10) version 1.9-1 only generated LXMX variable for the 5 and ignored the 10.
In version 1.10-1 LXMX variables are created for all values of winhr. This should explain that there are more output columns related to LXMX analyses in 1.10-1.

Part 4:
Some of the differences were discussed in this <https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=footer#!msg/rpackageggir/Q-0onVe_SZc/wp-zfNdvAgAJ> issue last week and I will include a fix in the next release. I did not expect this to affect any of the other part 4 and part 5 output variables, so will have a look where those difference come from.

Thanks,
Vincent

